    {
      "duration_ms": 10000,
      "caption": "inherit-product pulls in a parent; PRODUCT_PACKAGES += adds module names.",
      "narration": "In device.mk you call inherit-product with a parent path, then append module names to PRODUCT_PACKAGES. Both are plain make variables.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "heading",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "In device.mk",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 5,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 8,
          "at": 0,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "c",
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "make",
          "text": "$(call inherit-product, \\\n  $(SRC_TARGET_DIR)/product/ \\\n  core_64_bit.mk)\n\nPRODUCT_PACKAGES += \\\n    Launcher3",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 20,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 30,
          "at": 500,
          "enter": "slide-up"
        },
        {
          "id": "hl",
          "type": "highlight",
          "target": "c",
          "at": 4000,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "n",
          "type": "text",
          "text": "SRC_TARGET_DIR is build/make/target",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 58,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 10,
          "color": "gray",
          "at": 5500,
          "enter": "fade"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "duration_ms": 10000,
      "caption": "The graph is flattened: lists accumulate across files, scalars take the most-derived value.",
      "narration": "The build records parents in the node graph and flattens it. List variables like PRODUCT_PACKAGES accumulate across files, while scalars like PRODUCT_NAME take the most derived value.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "heading",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "Flattening rules",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 5,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 8,
          "at": 0,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "l",
          "type": "box",
          "text": "lists: PRODUCT_PACKAGES",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 20,
          "w": 40,
          "h": 10,
          "color": "green",
          "at": 500,
          "enter": "pop"
        },
        {
          "id": "s",
          "type": "box",
